      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ الْمَلَّاحِينَ وَ الْأَعْرَابِ هَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ تَقْصِيرٌ قَالَ لَا بُيُوتُهُمْ مَعَهُمْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Muhammad Bin Isa, from Yunus, from Is’haq Bin Ammar who said, ",
          "‘I asked him<sup>asws</sup> about the sailors and the Bedouins, ‘Is it upon them, the shortening (of the <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>)?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Are their houses not with them?’"
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "9. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Yunus from Ishaq ibn ‘Ammar who has said the following: “I once asked him (the Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of sailors and desert dwelling Arabs. Can they perform their Salah (prayer) as reduced? He (the Imam) said, ‘No, they cannot do so because their homes are with them.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
